{"id": "5fa51683586c7f2e0291667227ceb8fd", "text": "Rig Veda  which is considered the primordial group of hymns that gave rise \nto the entire  span of  Vedic literature. In that sense this chapter is like a \ncommentary on  the Purusha Sookta . This chapter also has a soulful prayer \nby Arjuna on seeing the Lord\u2019s universal form. While the Lord had \npreviously taught Arjuna about His greatness and attributes, the act of \nphysically seeing the Lord\u2019s universal form completely solidifies Arjuna\u2019s \nconviction in Sri Krishna\u2019s teachings.", "embedding": [-0.07227133214473724, 0.0006366728339344263, -0.08757981657981873, -0.017727147787809372, -0.09380824863910675, 0.046642083674669266, -0.004247212316840887, -0.04087572172284126, 0.04229259490966797, -0.03978230804204941, -0.03767627105116844, 0.032683346420526505, 0.024761324748396873, -0.09548725187778473, 0.014097334817051888, -0.013057779520750046, -0.05408060550689697, -6.55241310596466e-05, 0.05399350821971893, -0.021340060979127884, -0.04050320014357567, 0.0888066217303276, -0.016855305060744286, 0.01845814660191536, -0.06738351285457611, -0.01941591501235962, -0.010738587938249111, -0.0817054882645607, 0.03079974465072155, -0.06040995940566063, -0.04601099342107773, -0.01808544620871544, -0.05312255397439003, -0.05329839140176773, -0.04942306503653526, 0.09045778214931488, -0.03468252718448639, 0.0557495541870594, -0.08041385561227798, -0.04892329126596451, 0.0794999822974205, 0.04149794578552246, -0.06478266417980194, -0.01293842401355505, 0.06663839519023895, 0.001839245087467134, -0.040060702711343765, -0.011294015683233738, 0.040933702141046524, 0.020322971045970917, -0.048047274351119995, -0.04451809450984001, -0.04588920623064041, -0.0015193130820989609, 0.03853820264339447, -0.0018764605047181249, 0.05268171802163124, -0.0672733262181282, 0.07498452812433243, -0.01727267913520336, 0.022235244512557983, 0.07272919267416, 0.03584688529372215, 0.020313866436481476, 0.05786219611763954